      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In 52 patients with coronary artery disease the feasibility of performing first-pass cardiac studies with the short-lived tracer 195mAu was tested. Even with a currently available gamma camera, good results were obtained in terms of imaging quality, reproducibility and exercise response. The use of a multicrystal camera would, however, be desirable."},
